DECISION: shortcut_policy
VALUE:     option_A_zero_pad
RATIONALE: He et al. (2016b) CIFAR experiments use Option A (identity with zero-padding for extra channels, avg-pool for stride). Option B (1x1 projection) adds ~3.3K params per transition block. Option A keeps the network parameter-light and is the published reference. The base paper does not override this. Verified: PreAct-ResNet-110 PlainSkip param count is ~1.7M (passes test), consistent with published values for Option A.
------------------------------------------------------------------------
DECISION: lambda_at_downsampling_blocks
VALUE:     applied_uniformly
RATIONALE: Lambda-scaling and G normalisation apply to all blocks including stage-transition (downsampling) blocks. The base paper describes the skip variant as a per-block rule without any exception for downsampling blocks. Treating them differently would require an undocumented special case that is not defensible from the paper text. The shortcut tensor at downsampling blocks is the zero-padded identity (per shortcut_policy above); lambda then scales this zero-padded identity, which is mathematically consistent with the non-downsampling case.
------------------------------------------------------------------------
DECISION: weight_decay_scope
VALUE:     exclude_BN_LN_affine_and_bias
RATIONALE: BN/LN affine parameters (weight, bias) and all bias terms are excluded from weight decay. This is standard PyTorch practice and the most common published convention for ResNet training. Neither the base paper nor He et al. (2016b) state the scope explicitly. plan.md Section 8 flags this as a known risk; the default (exclude) is used here and logged. If reproduced numbers are systematically high by ~0.2-0.3 points, the alternative (include BN/LN/bias) should be tried.
------------------------------------------------------------------------
DECISION: figure3_block_range
VALUE:     stage2_all18blocks
RATIONALE: Figure 3 shows "middle depth" blocks. For PreAct-ResNet-110 (18 blocks/stage), Stage 2 (channels=32, spatial=16x16) is the complete middle stage. All 18 blocks in Stage 2 are used as the representative contiguous window. Block index 0 = first block of Stage 2 (the downsampling block from stage 1→2). This choice is unambiguous and reproducible from code. The paper's Figure 3 caption says "middle depth blocks" without specifying exact indices; Stage 2 is the natural middle of the 3-stage network.
------------------------------------------------------------------------
DECISION: table6_num_seeds
VALUE:     5_seeds
RATIONALE: The paper does not restate the run count for Table 6 (CIFAR-100, multi-depth). Per plan.md Section 5, 5 seeds are used for Table 6 as well, for consistency with Table 1 and to match the "Average of 5 runs" protocol stated for Table 1. This is the most defensible assumption and is noted here.
------------------------------------------------------------------------
DECISION: nesterov_momentum
VALUE:     false
RATIONALE: The config YAML specifies nesterov: false, following He et al. (2016b) which uses standard SGD momentum (not Nesterov). plan.md Section 5 notes "Nesterov = False (unless verified otherwise)." The base paper does not state otherwise. Standard momentum is used.
------------------------------------------------------------------------
DECISION: data_normalization_stats
VALUE:     recomputed_from_training_set
RATIONALE: Per plan.md Section 3 explicit requirement, per-channel mean/std are recomputed from the actual downloaded training batches (not hardcoded). The recomputed stats are written to results/logs/<dataset>_normstats.txt per run. Expected values: CIFAR-10 mean≈[0.4914,0.4822,0.4465] std≈[0.2470,0.2435,0.2616]; CIFAR-100 mean≈[0.5071,0.4865,0.4409] std≈[0.2673,0.2564,0.2762].
------------------------------------------------------------------------
