DECISION: 0.5xSkip_better_than_paper
VALUE:     accepted_as_fail
RATIONALE: 0.5xSkip achieved 11.85% test error (seeds: 11.96, 11.67, 11.92), significantly outperforming the paper's reported 18.61%. A hypothesis that gradient clipping artificially rescued it was tested and falsified: clipping only fired during the universal cold-start window (<2000 iters) and exactly zero times after iter 10,000 across all 3 seeds, meaning the variant optimized cleanly on its own without ongoing clipping intervention. The discrepancy is likely due to stronger baseline practices in this modern reproduction (e.g. shortcut_policy zero-pad, Kaiming init, lambda applied uniformly) rather than a bug. Per the strict +/-0.4 tolerance rule, it remains a FAIL, but will be reported honestly as a more stable trajectory rather than a broken codebase.
