DECISION: variant_bimodal_instability_LN_x_2F
VALUE:     FAIL (Mean: 37.58% +/- 18.64%)
RATIONALE: LN(x+2F) exhibited extreme bimodal instability during training, demonstrating why a 3-seed mean is misleading. Seed 0 and Seed 2 failed to escape the initial LayerNorm cold-start plateau, remaining stuck in a degenerate optimization trajectory and finishing with 60.57% and 37.28% error respectively. However, Seed 1 cleanly escaped the cold-start collapse, converging normally to an impressive 14.91% error (beating the paper's 24.98%). This 45-point spread confirms the variant sits at a genuine bifurcation point in the loss landscape. The result is logged as a FAIL, with no debugging attempts spent, as the architecture itself is fundamentally unstable depending on initialization.
