DECISION: report_integrity_correction
VALUE:     final_report_v1_table4_section_was_fabricated
RATIONALE: Closing verification (2026-08-18) revealed that the Table 4 section in
the previously generated FINAL_REPORT.md (written 2026-08-16) contained fabricated
per-seed values and incorrect means that do not exist in any JSON on disk. Specific
examples: seed-level values such as "5.37, 5.12, 5.16" for 1xSkip+BN were invented;
the reported paper target for 1xSkip+BN was listed as 7.06 instead of the correct
8.23. Additionally, Table 6 was entirely absent from the report despite all 30 runs
having completed. The raw training JSONs, all FINAL_*.csv files in results/tables/,
and the pipeline itself were verified to be internally consistent and trustworthy —
only the hand-authored markdown narrative was broken. Root cause: the final report
was authored by free-text generation rather than being mechanically rendered from the
verified CSVs. Corrective action: FINAL_REPORT.md has been regenerated from scratch
by a Python script that reads only the verified FINAL_*.csv files and the corrected
master table (ground-truth paper values cross-checked against the PDF). No numbers
were entered manually. This entry is logged per decisions.log discipline as an honest
record of a real report-integrity failure caught during closing review.
------------------------------------------------------------------------
------------------------------------------------------------------------
DECISION: verdict_logic_correction
VALUE:     pass_fail_now_uses_symmetric_abs_tolerance_0.40pp
RATIONALE: Closing review prep (2026-08-22) identified that generate_final_report.py
(v2, 2026-08-18) read from hand-authored FINAL_*.csv files whose verdict column
implemented directional logic — "FAIL (outperform)" vs "FAIL" as separate categories
— rather than the project's actual acceptance rule from plan.md Section 0: PASS iff
|reproduced - paper| <= 0.40 absolute percentage points, symmetric. As a result,
rows such as 1xSkip+LN (diff = +0.20, inside tolerance) were marked FAIL, and rows
such as 3xSkip (diff = -0.34, inside tolerance) were marked "FAIL (outperform)".
Fix: generate_final_report.py v3 (2026-08-22) reads from reproduced_table*_FINAL.csv
files produced by python -m src.evaluation.reproduce_tables, whose pass_fail column
is computed by src/evaluation/evaluate.py using the canonical rule
  pass_fail = "PASS" if abs_diff <= acceptance_tolerance else "FAIL"
where acceptance_tolerance = 0.40 is read from the YAML config. The script now
asserts that the count is exactly 14/32 PASS before writing any output, so any
future regression in the tolerance or CSV source will produce an immediate error
rather than a silently wrong report. This entry is in addition to (not replacing)
the existing report_integrity_correction entry.
------------------------------------------------------------------------
